Thanks Elias.   The last chapter of the R-INLA book is very helpful. I was thrown off by the use of the length of the index for, e.g., xi.field and u.field being used as 1: spde$n.spde.  I was taking it to be 1: n_x and 1:n_y etc...  My confusion.  So, I am assuming that both Zhi and u are  being treated spatially in the example given in book.  Is this correct?

Here is the model:
x_i = N(Zhi_i,    sig_x^2)
y_i  = N(b0 + b1*Zhi_i + u_i,   sig_e^2)    ## here i = j for simplicity

